.TH REMOTEBLE 1
.SH NAME
remoteble \- command-line client for a remote RemoteBLE agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remoteble
.RI [ global-options ] " command " [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B remoteble
controls Bluetooth Low Energy peripherals through a RemoteBLE agent. The client runs separately
from the host that owns the radio and communicates with the agent over an authenticated WebSocket.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config PATH
Read configuration from PATH.
.TP
.B --profile NAME
Select a named configuration profile.
.TP
.B --endpoint URL
Override the agent WebSocket endpoint.
.TP
.B --client-id ID
Override the persisted client identity used for lease resumption.
.TP
.B --token-stdin
Read the bearer token from standard input. It cannot be combined with a stdin write payload,
session, or shell.
.TP
.B --json
Emit one structured JSON envelope.
.TP
.B --jsonl
Emit newline-delimited structured JSON records.
.TP
.B --quiet
Emit only the primary value.
.TP
.B --output MODE
Select human, json, jsonl, hex, base64, raw, or quiet output where supported.
.TP
.B --log-level LEVEL
Select audit or debug operational logging.
.TP
.B --generate-completion SHELL
Generate a completion script for bash, fish, or zsh.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Show the CLI version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B agent status|capabilities|slots
Inspect agent state and negotiated capabilities.
.TP
.B scan
Discover advertisements. Supports --duration, --service, --name, --minimum-rssi, and --max-events.
.TP
.B connect, disconnect
Acquire or release a peripheral lease.
.TP
.B inspect
Discover a connected peripheral's GATT tree.
.TP
.B read
Read a characteristic.
.TP
.B descriptor read
Read a characteristic descriptor when the agent supports descriptors.
.TP
.B rssi
Read connected-link RSSI when the agent supports it.
.TP
.B observe
Stream characteristic notifications with --count, --timeout, or policy-gated --unbounded.
.TP
.B write
Write a characteristic only when both local advisory policy and agent-side enforcement permit it.
Use exactly one of --hex, --base64, --text, or --stdin, plus --write-type.
.TP
.B report
Show recent local audit records as a diagnostic report, including operations and their results.
.TP
.B session
Run the persistent JSONL machine-session protocol.
.TP
.B shell
Run the interactive human shell.
.TP
.B config show|validate
Inspect or validate effective configuration.
.TP
.B skills install|doctor
Install or verify the embedded portable Agent Skill locally. These commands do not require RemoteBLE
credentials or network access. Install defaults to user-scope auto detection; project scope requires
an explicit target. Doctor exits nonzero unless all selected copies are current.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REMOTE_BLE_TOKEN
Bearer token for the agent. The variable name can be changed in configuration.
.TP
.B REMOTE_BLE_CONFIG
Default configuration path.
.TP
.B REMOTE_BLE_LOG_DIR
Directory for audit and debug logs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I dist/completions/remoteble.bash
Bash completion shipped in release archives. Source it or install it in Bash's completion directory.
.TP
.I dist/completions/remoteble.zsh
Zsh completion.
.TP
.I dist/completions/remoteble.fish
Fish completion.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means success. Usage errors exit 2, authentication errors exit 4, missing peripherals exit 5,
lease contention exits 6, policy or unsupported operations exit 7, indeterminate writes exit 8,
and retryable transport failures exit 9.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full command and JSON schema reference is distributed with the project documentation.
